    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "The whole frai-core suite now passes: 8 files, 28 tests. I changed only source files, and no test files were touched.\n\nThere were two separate source bugs:\n\n- **Governance test** (`src/finetune/index.js`): `APPROVAL_STATUSES` was imported but never exported by name, so the test read `undefined.join`. I added a named re-export of `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS` and `RISK_LEVELS`. The default export is unchanged.\n- **Eval test** (`src/eval/metrics.js`): `runEvaluations` calls every default metric as `metric(outputs, references)`. `toxicityMetric`'s second parameter is the banned-term list, so the references were treated as banned words and \"Hello\" was flagged, giving a score of 0. The default metric list now wraps toxicity so it only receives the outputs. `toxicityMetric` itself is unchanged, so direct callers that pass a banned-term list still work.\n\nI didn't check `git status` because that command needed approval, so I haven't confirmed the exact diff. I haven't committed anything.",
